0..76 Comment "//! The strings subject\'s shared declarations, imported by every source that"
77..155 Comment "//! reads them (`import \"./string-base.gandr\";`): where a string\'s bytes live,"
156..236 Comment "//! and the byte lists every claim reads and builds. A string is a value: a copy"
237..301 Comment "//! is a new string, and no write to one is seen through another"
302..378 Comment "//! [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]. Short"
379..458 Comment "//! strings keep their bytes inline and long ones share a buffer until a write,"
459..515 Comment "//! as the C++ and Rust small-string representations do."
516..519 Comment "//!"
520..598 Comment "//! - cites: [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]"
599..602 Comment "//!"
603..787 Comment "//! [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]: https://doi.org/10.5381/jot.2022.21.2.a2 \"Racordon et al., Implementation strategies for mutable value semantics\""
